/*  EXPECTED: REJECTED at type-check, identically by both backends.
    A table made in the rabbit is given an outer series AFTER a rabbit's series is stored into its first element, in a loop.

    A name records where the NAME was made; the store is judged against where what it reaches
    was made, which can be further out. Judged once everything is checked, so a later statement
    that lowers it counts too (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, obligation O2). */

Define keeper as a series of series of number.
Insert (a series of number with (0)) into keeper.
Pull a rabbit.
    Define bag as a series of series of series of number.
    Define round as 0.
    While round is less than 2, repeat:
        Increment round by 1.
        Define inner as a series of number with (1, 2, 3).
        If the number of bag is greater than 0:
            Insert inner into item 1 of bag.
        Done.
        Insert keeper into bag.
    Done.
Done.
State keeper.
